speechtext:
One of the Conservatives says he did not get to it. He made some suggestions. I will not comment on those;
1 thought they were illustrations of fundamental Conservative thought, if that is not a contradiction in terms. The suggestions that were made were exactly of the same kind of tinkering nature that we have had from the Liberals.
On the other hand, he suggested some restrictions should be put on tourists with regard to what they bring into the country. That is one idea. On the other hand, there was the suggestion of imposing for a brief period of time some tariffs, thereby holding out some prospect that jobs will not be lost by keeping out certain products. That is a clear violation of an international agreement. Those were the two principal suggestions from the Conservatives. It is entirely the same kind of tinkering as that proposed by the Liberal party. There is no difference at all.
